    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A charming period home enjoying sea views\n\nSea View occupies an enviable position at the end of a terrace on Sea Road, directly facing The Priests Beach and open to an outlook that few homes along this coastline can rival. Across the road lies a well-regarded sea swimming location, and the Cooley Mountains form a compelling backdrop to the north-east. The home extends to 124.9 sq m, is available immediately, and carries the kind of unhurried character that comes with a well-kept, established property — with some original period features lending warmth and texture throughout.\n\nAt ground level, the accommodation flows from a generous kitchen and breakfast room through to a formal dining room that readily adapts to a home office or reading room, a comfortable sitting room, a utility room, and a guest WC. The layout is practical and well-proportioned, with each room serving a clear purpose without feeling contrived. A large landing or office area at upper level adds valuable flexible space, particularly suited to those working from home or in need of a quiet study. \n\nAll four bedrooms are positioned to benefit from sea views, a distinction that sets the property apart from comparable properties in the area. Waking to open water each morning is not a secondary benefit here — it is the defining quality of the home. A family bathroom serves the upper floor, and the overall condition of the accommodation means a new owner can settle in without delay, while still having scope to add their own mark over time.\n\nOutside, a private rear garden offers a sunny and sheltered seating area, well away from passing traffic and not overlooked. Parking to the side of the house is a practical asset in a coastal village setting. The combination of outlook, orientation, village position, and ready availability makes Sea View a genuinely compelling prospect for those seeking a lifestyle change, a considered downsizer move, or a coastal base within realistic reach of Dublin and Belfast."
      },
